Package: survlearning
Type: Package
Title: Unified Statistical Learning for Survival and Reliability
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(person("Pedro Luiz", "Ramos", email = "pedro.ramos@uc.cl",
    role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Hemant", "Ishwaran", role = "ctb", comment = "Included RF-SRC code"),
    person("Udaya B.", "Kogalur", role = "ctb", comment = "Included RF-SRC code"),
    person("Christopher", "Jackson", role = "ctb", comment = "Adapted Royston-Parmar initialization"),
    person("Aaron J.", "Molstad", role = "ctb", comment = "Adapted Gehan ADMM"),
    person("Piotr M.", "Suder", role = "ctb", comment = "Adapted Gehan ADMM"))
Description: Provides a small formula-based interface for fitting, tuning,
    predicting, and comparing statistical learning models for right-censored
    survival and reliability data. Provides censoring-aware evaluation,
    reusable stratified, grouped and temporal validation, and nested tuning.
    Distinguishes risk scores, survival probabilities and median survival
    times. Includes reference models, forests, boosting and neural survival
    models through integrated engines, with training-only preprocessing and
    explicit prediction capabilities.
